  "excelListParent": "Belongs to",
  "excelNotice": "Import rules for the IA cave à vin workbook\n\nSheet and column names stay in French, so a workbook works whatever the app language.\n\nSheet “Vins”: one row per wine (producer, cuvée, vintage).\n- Column id filled in: the existing wine is updated. Empty id: a wine is created.\n- Action = SUPPRIMER (with the id): the wine is removed from the cellar, its movements stay in the history.\n- Domaine, Pays, Couleur and Millésime are required. Millésime: a year, or NM for a non-vintage wine.\n- Lists (country, region, appellation, grapes, pairings…) take the values of the “Listes” sheet. Several values in one cell: separated by a semicolon.\n- Grapes: “Merlot 80 %; Cabernet Franc 20 %”, 100% in total at most.\n- The columns Origine garde, Statut garde, Statut enrichissement, Note Parker, Meilleure note, Stock total and Photo principale are calculated: they are ignored on import.\n\nSheet “Lots”: one row per lot (same wine, size, owner, location, price).\n- Lot id filled in: update; empty: creation. Action = SUPPRIMER: the lot is deleted.\n- Wine id: the id of a wine in the “Vins” sheet, or #row number for a wine created by the same import (example: #12).\n- Quantité: target quantity. The app creates an adjustment movement for the difference, reason “import Excel”. Empty cell: stock unchanged.\n- Emplacement: full path, for example “Cave > Armoire 1 > Casier A”.\n\nSheet “Mouvements”: read-only, ignored on import.\n\nPhotos: attach a zip of photos; a photo whose name appears in the Photo principale column is linked to the wine.\n\nBefore any import, the app runs a dry run and shows a report. An automatic backup is made just before, and the import is applied in full or not at all.",
